This product includes material derived from the Phil project
(https://github.com/abiggerhammer/phil), licensed under the Apache License 2.0:

- core/src/keywords.json: keyword descriptions from docs/reference/keywords-phase1.md.
- core/src/reserved.json: the Grammar-v1 reserved-word list from the Phil lexer.
- The lexer, parser and highlighting grammar are independent implementations
  written from grammar/phase1-surface.ebnf.
- The "Ping" example follows the program in Phil's tutorial.

- docs/playground/philc.wasm: the `philc` executable from the Phil repository, compiled
  unmodified to WebAssembly by .github/workflows/philc-wasm.yml. The exact Phil commit is
  recorded in philc/build.json. The binary also contains the GHC runtime and the Haskell
  libraries philc depends on (base, text, containers, bytestring, megaparsec,
  cryptohash-sha256 and their dependencies), each under its own BSD-style licence.

The playground bundles @bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim (MIT OR Apache-2.0) to run that binary.

